Tārā kisses dead Vālin face and laments --- Tārā reproaches Vālin ignoring counsel preferring earth --- Tārā mourns helpless widowhood and stone unburst heart --- Tārā declares widowhood despite sons and riches --- Tārā shrinks from embracing blood-dust body --- Tārā credits Rāma shaft for Sugrīva triumph --- Nīla draws shaft releasing blood streams --- Tārā bathes dusted husband with tears and presents Aṅgada --- Aṅgada grasps father feet seeking blessing in vain --- Tārā notes missing Indra garland yet abiding glory sharing ruin with son
